"""The {{ module_title }} module's public facade.

The only file another module may import from this one. Everything else here --
the domain, the use cases, storage -- is private, and `jfast contracts check`
rejects an import of it from outside.

Three rules keep this file worth having:

* **It returns DTOs, never a row.** A row carries its session and its lazy
  relations across the boundary, and every column becomes part of the API the
  day someone reads it.
* **It takes the caller's session and an explicit tenant_id.** The read joins
  the caller's transaction instead of opening a second one, and the tenant is
  an argument rather than something inferred from a request that a worker or
  another module does not have.
* **Queries only.** To make another module react to something that happened
  here, publish an event through the outbox; do not call back into it.

The payoff comes later: when this module becomes its own service, this file
becomes an HTTP client with the same signatures, and no caller changes.

A caller declares the dependency in contracts.toml:

    [modules.<caller>]
    depends_on = ["{{ module }}"]
"""

{% set read_from = "entity" %}
{% set repository_import = "from .storage import " ~ Module ~ "Repository" %}
{% set fetch = "row = await " ~ Module ~ "Repository(session, tenant_id=tenant_id).get(" ~ module ~ "_id)\n    entity = row.to_domain() if row is not None else None" %}
{% set fetch_note = "# A read goes through storage and crosses into the domain at to_domain(),\n    # the same seam every use case reads through. A write added here calls the\n    # use case in use_cases/, so the rules run whoever asked." %}
{% include "_module_shared/public_body.j2" %}
